                <pb facs="1013" n="985" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg985"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/10–953: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lodge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-10-09T20:34:00-05:00">October 9,
                            1953—8:34 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Delga 96. Subject: Japanese associate membership. Sawada advised Key that his
                    government had decided not to apply for an associate membership and to hold this
                    matter in abeyance for the remainder of the current session inasmuch as
                    discussion of the membership question in the <hi rendition="#italic">ad hoc</hi>
                    committee was nearing its end. His government would, however, re-examine the
                    question prior to the opening of the ninth session in the light of international
                    conditions then existing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lodge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
